.TH WERKMEISTER-ISSUE 1 "" "werkmeister" "Werkmeister Manual"
.SH NAME
werkmeister\-issue \- Read, update or file an issue in this machine's issue tracker (see \fBwerkmeister setup\fR)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBwerkmeister issue\fR <action> [ref]
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
view, ready: print JSON
.TP
\fB\-\-status <name>\fR
update: move the issue to this status
.TP
\fB\-\-comment <text>\fR
update: add this comment
.TP
\fB\-\-project <key>\fR
create: the Jira project key to file in; ready: a project from projects: in config.yaml
.TP
\fB\-\-type <type>\fR
create: bug, feature or task (mapped to the tracker's issue type)
.TP
\fB\-\-title <text>\fR
create: the issue's summary
.TP
\fB\-\-body\-file <path>\fR
create: the issue's description, from a file (\- for stdin)
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Reads or updates one issue in this machine's tracker (\fBwerkmeister setup\fR picks it).
.IP \(bu 3
\fBview\fR prints the issue's briefing; \fB\-\-json\fR prints it as JSON.
.IP \(bu 3
\fBupdate\fR moves its status and/or adds a comment; at least one is required.
.IP \(bu 3
\fBcreate\fR files a new issue and prints its URL. Only trackers with an API path (Jira); file GitHub issues with \fBgh issue create\fR.
.IP \(bu 3
\fBstart\fR moves the workspace's issue to in progress, forward only. It exits 0 when the tracker refuses, so a stage never fails on it.
.IP \(bu 3
\fBready\fR lists a project's open work in priority order: its board's ready column, else the open issues.
.PP
Inside a workspace the issue reference can be left out: it is read from \fB.werkmeister/workspace.yml\fR.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
werkmeister issue view
werkmeister issue update \-\-status "In Review" \-\-comment "PR opened"
werkmeister issue create \-\-project SW \-\-type bug \-\-title "Short summary" \-\-body\-file body.md
werkmeister issue ready \-\-json
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBwerkmeister\fR(1)
